  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Probability mass function and distribution function"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "For a discrete X, the probability mass function (p.m.f.) $p(x) = P(X = x)$ satisfies $p(x) \\ge 0$ and $\\sum p(x) = 1$. The table of values and probabilities is the probability distribution. The distribution function (c.d.f.) is $F(x) = P(X \\le x) = \\sum_{t \\le x} p(t)$; it rises in steps from 0 to 1."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "p(x) ≥ 0, Σp(x) = 1"
    },
    {
     "en": "F(x) = P(X ≤ x), non-decreasing"
    },
    {
     "en": "F(−∞) = 0, F(∞) = 1"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The probability mass function gives P of X equal to x; the values are non-negative and add up to one. The distribution function F of x is P of X less than or equal to x.",
    "kn": "ಸಂಭವನೀಯತಾ ದ್ರವ್ಯರಾಶಿ ಫಲನ p(x) = P(X = x); ಮೌಲ್ಯಗಳು ಋಣವಲ್ಲ, ಮೊತ್ತ 1. ವಿತರಣಾ ಫಲನ F(x) = P(X ≤ x)."
   },
   "formula": "F(x) = P(X \\le x) = \\sum_{t \\le x} p(t)"
  },
